{
  "$schema": "../../../src/data/docs-authoring-schema.json",
  "id": "math-noise-fields",
  "title": "Math utilities, noise and spatial fields",
  "group": "Mathematics",
  "summary": "Use vectors, matrices, noise and spatial fields to describe motion and procedural geometry.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "vector-and-matrix-foundations",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Vector and matrix foundations"
        },
        {
          "type": "tabs",
          "tabs": [
            {
              "label": "Vector addition",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "example",
                  "example": "labs/pg-vector-addition"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "label": "Quaternion",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "example",
                  "example": "labs/pg-quaternion-rotation"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "label": "AABB",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "example",
                  "example": "labs/pg-bounding-box"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Vec2/Vec3, Point, Quaternion, Mat3/Mat4 and AABB provide engine-native mathematics and typed-array views. Some operations mutate and return the receiver while others produce a new object. Read the specific method contract before reusing a scratch vector. Singular matrix inversion and zero quaternion inversion are explicit failure cases."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Exact contracts: [Vec2](/api-math-vector#vec2), [Vec3](/api-math-vector#vec3), [Point](/api-math-vector#point), [Quaternion](/api-math-vector#quaternion), [Mat3](/api-math-vector#mat3), [Mat4](/api-math-vector#mat4), [AABB](/api-math#aabb)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fourier-reconstruction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Fourier reconstruction"
        },
        {
          "type": "tabs",
          "tabs": [
            {
              "label": "Reconstruction",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "example",
                  "example": "labs/pg-fourier-reconstruction"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "FourierTransform computes discrete Fourier coefficients for sampled 2D complex coordinates and supports epicycle reconstruction. Sample a path consistently, choose coefficient ordering intentionally and balance truncation against visible detail. A finite set of coefficients approximates the source, with ringing and sampling artifacts near sharp corners."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Exact contracts: [FourierTransform](/api-math#fouriertransform)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "noise-generators",
      "blocks": [
