            {
              "label": "WhiteNoise",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "example",
                  "example": "labs/pg-noise-whitenoise"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "label": "WorleyNoise",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "example",
                  "example": "labs/pg-noise-worleynoise"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The math/noise directory contains seeded procedural noise implementations and utilities. Choose a generator based on its dimensionality, continuity, repeatability and output range. A seed stabilizes the noise field; the sampling coordinate determines whether it stays attached to local geometry or moves through world space."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Noise used for static geometry should remain in the same coordinate system across frames. For motion, animate a coordinate/phase smoothly instead of selecting a new unrelated random field every frame."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "All noise classes and their exact sample/seed methods appear in the math/noise API."
        }
      ]
    },
